  "description_text": "In every neighborhood there's a block that is the one'' that makes you want to move there immediately. Unfortunately, there are only so many homes on that block. Fortunately, 17 Bennington's cheery faade, sheltered by a front garden is ready to welcome you home. Originally built in the aftermath of the 1906 earthquake, and substantially renovated 100 years later since 2006, this home is ready for modern life. With 9 useful rooms in total, there's space for music, home offices, workshops and privacy, while the large double parlor and kitchen/dining room make space for life together too. The creativity that can come from having the right space cannot be underestimated - one current owner is a sculptor and musician and the other is locally famous for her lego machines that automatically hand out candy on Halloween. What will you do here? If that's kick back on the deck with friends that's fine, but you might just find yourself inspired The home has the perfect floorplan too. Main level has one bedroom, one bath, double parlor, spacious kitchen/dining room that flows to the rear garden. Upstairs there's a primary with a bath, a full bath and a third bedroom. Downstairs there is a fourth bedroom, storage/laundry and a music room/office and direct access to the garage with parking for one smaller car.",
